WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:03.360
Creepy, kooky, mysterious, spooky.

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:07.480
Netflix's "Wednesday" is all these things
and more, and is mostly very successful at

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:10.210
mixing genuine scares with morbid humor.

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:13.170
But every once in a while, it doesn't quite
nail it.

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:16.850
These are the hit series' biggest hits and
misses.

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:21.441
Wednesday Addams is undoubtedly one of the
most beloved characters of the "Addams Family" franchise.

00:00:21.441 --> 00:00:26.010
Her deadpan expressions and love of all things
macabre are oddly endearing traits that have

00:00:26.010 --> 00:00:27.380
made her an American icon.

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:32.850
After the character was portrayed by Christina
Ricci in the 1991 and 1993 Barry Sonnenfeld

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:37.222
movies, whoever would take on the mantle of
Wednesday would have some massive shoes to fill.

00:00:37.222 --> 00:00:41.300
Thankfully, Jenna Ortega is the perfect choice
for the gothic Cinderella.

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:45.080
Ortega captures the spirit and look of Wednesday
Addams perfectly, from her black-and-white

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:49.050
outfits to her grim expression and spot-on,
sardonic delivery.

00:00:49.050 --> 00:00:54.320
"Lurch, please remind my parents that I'm
no longer speaking to them."

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:58.260
She delivers plenty of memorable moments,
including taking revenge on the swim team

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:02.580
for bullying her brother Pugsley by dropping
a school of bloodthirsty piranhas into the

00:01:02.580 --> 00:01:03.620
swimming pool.

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:07.530
In another hilarious scene, Wednesday is forced
to volunteer at the local pilgrim theme park

00:01:07.530 --> 00:01:09.470
for the school's outreach program.

00:01:09.470 --> 00:01:13.430
Dressed in colonial garb, she informs a group
of tourists that the fudge they are sampling

00:01:13.430 --> 00:01:18.180
is made from cacao beans "procured by the
oppressed indigenous people of the Amazon."

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:19.180
She adds,

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:22.890
"All proceeds go to uphold this pathetic whitewashing
of American history."

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:26.909
While we'll always have a place in our hearts
for Ricci's Wednesday, Ortega's portrayal

00:01:26.909 --> 00:01:29.220
lives up to the legend.

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:33.720
The biggest mystery in "Wednesday" involves
a creature called a Hyde, which terrorizes

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:36.729
the small town of Jericho and the Nevermore
school.

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:40.310
Wednesday discovers that the Hyde is actually
a human who transforms into the ferocious

00:01:40.310 --> 00:01:44.490
beast, and that their abilities were unlocked
by someone who is now controlling them.

00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:48.310
Wednesday is determined to find out the monster's
true identity, as well as the person pulling

00:01:48.310 --> 00:01:49.500
the strings.

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:53.470
Wednesday deduces that the person helping
the hyde is Laurel Gates, the younger sister

00:01:53.470 --> 00:01:58.689
of Garett Gates, who suffered a fatal accident
at the time Wednesday's parents attended Nevermore.

00:01:58.689 --> 00:02:00.760
Laurel is hiding her true identity, however.

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:04.549
"Laurel was presumed drowned, but no body
was ever recovered."

00:02:04.549 --> 00:02:08.610
At one point, Wednesday is visiting her friend
Eugene in the hospital when her court-ordered

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:12.670
therapist, Dr. Valerie Kinbott, arrives with
a vase of flowers.

00:02:12.670 --> 00:02:17.235
After Wednesday leaves, Kinbott neatly arranges
the vase filled with pale pink roses on a table.

00:02:17.235 --> 00:02:21.430
The camera focuses for a long moment on the
flowers, so clearly, they're important.

00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:26.280
Sure enough, when Wednesday, Enid, and Tyler
stake out the old Gates house, they find Laurel's

00:02:26.280 --> 00:02:30.569
old room recently lived in and decorated with
the pink roses from the hospital.

00:02:30.569 --> 00:02:34.209
This leads Wednesday to believe that Kinbott
is actually the missing Laurel Gates.

00:02:34.209 --> 00:02:38.090
But it all fits a little too neatly, and the
fact that the hospital scene seems to linger

00:02:38.090 --> 00:02:42.170
a little too long on the roses makes it all
too clear that this is a classic, and perhaps

00:02:42.170 --> 00:02:45.470
too-obvious misdirection.

00:02:45.470 --> 00:02:48.450
Director Tim Burton has always had a unique
view of the world.

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:52.730
Throughout his most notable features, such
as "Edward Scissorhands," "Beetlejuice," "Frankenweenie,"

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:57.340
and 1989's "Batman," Burton's art reflects
his tendency to see the world from a gleefully

00:02:57.340 --> 00:02:59.070
morbid perspective.

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:04.480
"If you gotta go, go with a smile!"

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:08.530
It's a wonder that it took so long for him
to deliver his own take on "The Addams Family"

00:03:08.530 --> 00:03:12.920
franchise, because it seems to fit him like
a pair of lacy Victorian gloves.

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:16.840
Burton directs four of the eight episodes
of "Wednesday," and his trademark gothic aesthetic

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:18.480
is present throughout.

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:22.629
Wednesday's monochromatic attire is highlighted
by various hints of color, such as the stained

00:03:22.629 --> 00:03:26.920
glass window in her dorm room that she shares
with her werewolf roommate, Enid.

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:30.790
Enid's bright personality is reflected in
her fashion, and the window on her side of

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:32.520
the room is painted in bright colors.

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:37.390
Wednesday's side, meanwhile, is colorless
and bleak, as is her half of the large window.

00:03:37.390 --> 00:03:41.420
Wednesday is even fitted with her own custom
black Nevermore Academy uniform, as she is

00:03:41.420 --> 00:03:43.590
apparently allergic to color.

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:47.390
It isn't just Wednesday Addams' look that
gets the Tim Burton treatment.

00:03:47.390 --> 00:03:51.489
Nevermore Academy itself, with its gothic
architecture and shadowy recesses are also

00:03:51.489 --> 00:03:53.920
reminiscent of Burton's previous work.

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:58.489
The design of the Hyde monster is also distinctly
Burtonesque, with its wide, bulging eyes and

00:03:58.489 --> 00:04:00.890
rows of razor-sharp teeth.

00:04:00.890 --> 00:04:04.819
In her psychic visions, Wednesday is able
to communicate with the spirit of her ancestor,

00:04:04.819 --> 00:04:06.170
Goody Addams.

00:04:06.170 --> 00:04:10.480
Wednesday and Goody look almost identical,
and Goody is also played by Ortega.

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:14.390
We learn that Goody was a powerful witch who,
like Wednesday, had visions.

00:04:14.390 --> 00:04:19.040
She was a sworn enemy of Jericho's oppressive
founder, Joseph Crackstone, whose hatred of

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:21.180
outcasts was all-consuming.

00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:26.000
In a truly despicable act, Crackstone gathered
all Jericho's outcasts, locked them in a barn,

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:29.630
and had it set on fire, leaving everyone inside
to burn alive.

00:04:29.630 --> 00:04:33.650
Goody would later curse Crackstone's remains
so that he could never rise again.

00:04:33.650 --> 00:04:37.980
Many viewers might just dismiss the name "Goody"
as an old-fashioned sign of the times.

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:41.949
But anyone who is knowledgeable about early
American history or of Arthur Miller's play

00:04:41.949 --> 00:04:45.950
"The Crucible" might raise their eyebrows
at this one, because "Goody" isn't a name

00:04:45.950 --> 00:04:47.000
at all.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:48.000
It's a title.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:52.680
Thought Co. confirms that in the 17th century,
Goody was a title for a married woman.

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:56.520
It was short for "goodwife," and would be
equivalent to today's use of "Mrs."

00:04:56.520 --> 00:05:00.639
There is no mention of Goody Addams being
married, and though it is possible that this

00:05:00.639 --> 00:05:03.240
was the case, the show's writers don't clarify.

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:07.250
So we're left to assume that Goody is actually
intended to be her first name.

00:05:07.250 --> 00:05:08.660
Wednesday even says it's her name.

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:11.919
"Her name is Goody Addams."

00:05:11.919 --> 00:05:16.400
At the heart of Season 1 of Netflix's "Wednesday"
is a supernatural murder mystery involving

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:20.480
a bloodthirsty monster, a dark prophecy, and
a classic cover-up scheme.

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:23.539
It all makes Wednesday's time at Nevermore
very memorable.

00:05:23.539 --> 00:05:28.280
It all begins when a gargoyle statue nearly
crushes Wednesday, and it's clearly no accident.

00:05:28.280 --> 00:05:32.370
The murder attempt is thwarted when fellow
student Xavier Thorpe pushes Wednesday out

00:05:32.370 --> 00:05:33.920
of the way just in time.

00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:38.090
It turns out that a fellow student with telekinetic
abilities named Rowan believes that Wednesday

00:05:38.090 --> 00:05:41.530
is the source of a prophecy that foretells
Nevermore's doom.

00:05:41.530 --> 00:05:45.910
When Rowan attempts to attack Wednesday directly,
he is killed by a terrifying monster who then

00:05:45.910 --> 00:05:47.979
disappears into the shadows.

00:05:47.979 --> 00:05:51.630
Like the teen detective in the novel she is
writing, Wednesday takes it upon herself to

00:05:51.630 --> 00:05:54.910
uncover the seedy machinations happening at
Nevermore Academy.

00:05:54.910 --> 00:05:59.130
She discovers not only the dark history of
the town of Jericho and the real origin of

00:05:59.130 --> 00:06:04.060
the Hyde, but the secret that her parents,
Gomez and Morticia, have been hiding for years.

00:06:04.060 --> 00:06:08.280
"Wednesday" throws viewers for a loop as each
episode reveals more of the bigger picture

00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:12.120
and ends with a truly surprising twist.

00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:16.180
It's sad to say that the "Wednesday" series
uses the hackneyed trope in which the competitive,

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:19.720
popular girl can't stand the presence of the
weird new girl and makes it her mission to

00:06:19.720 --> 00:06:20.970
take her down.

00:06:20.970 --> 00:06:25.310
Bianca Barclay is the most popular girl at
Nevermore Academy, as well as a siren with

00:06:25.310 --> 00:06:28.710
the power to use her voice to exert her influence
over others.

00:06:28.710 --> 00:06:33.030
Bianca is arrogant and territorial, and Wednesday
takes issue with Bianca's bullying.

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:37.160
The moment Bianca and Wednesday meet, there
is an immediate animosity between them.

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:41.210
When Wednesday volunteers to spar with Bianca
in fencing class, their exchange is dripping

00:06:41.210 --> 00:06:42.210
with contempt.

00:06:42.210 --> 00:06:44.370
"You must be the psychopath they let in."

00:06:44.370 --> 00:06:47.060
"And you must be the self-appointed queen
bee.

00:06:47.060 --> 00:06:50.530
Interesting thing about bees — pull out
their stingers and they drop dead."

00:06:50.530 --> 00:06:55.129
The rivalry between Wednesday and Bianca covers
all the cliches, down to the two girls eventually

00:06:55.129 --> 00:06:57.370
learning to sympathize and become allies.

00:06:57.370 --> 00:07:00.130
The problem isn't that there's conflict between
the characters.

00:07:00.130 --> 00:07:03.620
The way it happens is just a little played
out.

00:07:03.620 --> 00:07:07.759
The handy Thing plays a big role in Netflix's
"Wednesday" as the title character's sidekick

00:07:07.759 --> 00:07:09.069
and confidante.

00:07:09.069 --> 00:07:13.605
Although he's sent by her parents to snoop
on her, Wednesday recruits Thing for her own service.

00:07:13.605 --> 00:07:18.479
Thanks to his quick fingers and small stature,
Thing can get in and out of most places unseen,

00:07:18.479 --> 00:07:20.139
making him the perfect spy.

00:07:20.139 --> 00:07:22.830
Thing absolutely steals every scene he's in.

00:07:22.830 --> 00:07:27.629
Even though he's just a hand, performer Victor
Dorobantu, is able to convey the most complex

00:07:27.629 --> 00:07:28.629
of emotions.

00:07:28.629 --> 00:07:32.379
We can feel his grudging anger at Wednesday
as he indifferently flips through the pages

00:07:32.379 --> 00:07:33.490
of a magazine.

00:07:33.490 --> 00:07:37.650
We can also discern his casual smugness as
he sits on the railing of Wednesday's bed,

00:07:37.650 --> 00:07:41.780
swinging his fingers back and forth like legs
as he presents the dress he stole for her.

00:07:41.780 --> 00:07:44.930
Thing also has a really strong character,
even though he can't speak.

00:07:44.930 --> 00:07:48.740
He clearly cares about Wednesday, and his
loyalty is unshakable, even when he doesn't

00:07:48.740 --> 00:07:50.169
agree with her actions.

00:07:50.169 --> 00:07:53.720
In the episode where Wednesday finds Thing
impaled and bleeding to death, we couldn't

00:07:53.720 --> 00:07:55.440
help but feel a sense of panic.

00:07:55.440 --> 00:07:59.389
Uncle Fester is able to save Thing using his
electromagnetic powers, but the buildup to

00:07:59.389 --> 00:08:03.639
that moment is one of the tensest of the series,
because viewers have built such an attachment

00:08:03.639 --> 00:08:05.129
to Thing.

00:08:05.129 --> 00:08:08.800
Once Wednesday and Bianca set aside their
differences at the dance, the series begins

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:10.800
to show Bianca in a new light.

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:16.525
At Nevermore Academy's Parents Weekend, Bianca's
mother, a siren named Gabrielle, shows up unexpectedly.

00:08:16.525 --> 00:08:20.629
We learn that Gabrielle is a member of a cult
called MorningSong, which Bianca has recently

00:08:20.629 --> 00:08:21.629
escaped from.

00:08:21.629 --> 00:08:26.139
They argue over Bianca's return to the fold,
with Gabrielle threatening to reveal the secret

00:08:26.139 --> 00:08:28.830
about how Bianca made it into Nevermore.

00:08:28.830 --> 00:08:32.430
Bianca later promises her mother to return
to MorningSong at the end of the semester,

00:08:32.430 --> 00:08:34.529
but makes an interesting claim about the return.

00:08:34.529 --> 00:08:41.200
"But after this, you and MorningSong are out
of my life…forever."

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:44.769
It's fair to assume that the show will attempt
to delve deeper into Bianca's character and

00:08:44.769 --> 00:08:50.029
MorningSong in its second season, but in the
context of the first season, it's pretty disappointing.

00:08:50.029 --> 00:08:53.690
The show wraps up the subplot fairly quickly,
which makes it feel like little more than

00:08:53.690 --> 00:08:54.880
time filler.

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:58.100
Of course, we can't predict what the plot
for "Wednesday" Season 2 might be if it gets

00:08:58.100 --> 00:09:02.410
picked up, so it is possible that MorningSong
might be a new source of conflict for Wednesday

00:09:02.410 --> 00:09:04.470
and her friends in the future.

00:09:04.470 --> 00:09:08.420
The first name of the Addams Family's father
being Gomez seems to imply that his side of

00:09:08.420 --> 00:09:10.440
the family is of Hispanic descent.

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:14.360
The Barry Sonnenfeld films of the '90s ran
with this concept, casting Puerto Rican actor

00:09:14.360 --> 00:09:16.610
Raul Julia as the patriarch.

00:09:16.610 --> 00:09:21.380
This idea continued with the release of the
2019 animated film, with Guatemalan-born actor

00:09:21.380 --> 00:09:24.130
Oscar Isaac providing Gomez's voice.

00:09:24.130 --> 00:09:28.310
Netflix embraced this idea even further, casting
Jenna Ortega, who is of Mexican and Puerto

00:09:28.310 --> 00:09:33.820
Richan descent, in the titular role, as well
as Puerto Rican actor Luis Guzmán as Gomez.

00:09:33.820 --> 00:09:37.560
"Wednesday" isn't the first to add diversity
to the "Addams Family'' franchise, but it

00:09:37.560 --> 00:09:41.029
is the first to cast a Latina actor to play
the goth teen.

00:09:41.029 --> 00:09:44.120
The show acknowledges Wednesday's heritage
in various other ways.

00:09:44.120 --> 00:09:48.440
In her dorm room, Wednesday often listens
to Spanish-language music on her Victrola.

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:53.180
It's also established that Gomez's family,
including his ancestor Goody, came from Mexico.

00:09:53.180 --> 00:09:56.820
In another episode, Wednesday mentions that
her family keeps up their ofrenda all year

00:09:56.820 --> 00:10:00.970
long for Día de los Muertos, the Mexican
Day of the Dead.

00:10:00.970 --> 00:10:04.740
For better or for worse, there are certain
parallels between the outcasts of Netflix's

00:10:04.740 --> 00:10:07.560
"Wednesday" and the LGBTQ+ community.

00:10:07.560 --> 00:10:10.930
Being different is a challenge for anyone,
but it can be even more difficult when people

00:10:10.930 --> 00:10:13.950
have false preconceived notions about who
you are.

00:10:13.950 --> 00:10:17.940
For the students and faculty of Nevermore,
prejudice is an ongoing concern from the local

00:10:17.940 --> 00:10:19.150
citizens of Jericho.

00:10:19.150 --> 00:10:24.229
A local group of "normie" boys frequently
delights in causing trouble for the outcast kids.

00:10:24.229 --> 00:10:28.660
They terrorize the awkward Eugene during the
town's Outreach Day, as well as pull an elaborate

00:10:28.660 --> 00:10:31.390
prank to ruin the school's Rave'N Dance.

00:10:31.390 --> 00:10:36.120
Even Jericho's mayor, despite outwardly claiming
to want a peaceful co-existence with Nevermore,

00:10:36.120 --> 00:10:37.720
has his own misgivings.

00:10:37.720 --> 00:10:41.459
Given the similarities between the outcasts
in "Wednesday" and the real-life struggles

00:10:41.459 --> 00:10:46.760
of LGBTQ+ people, it's a shame that the series
is sadly lacking in queer representation.

00:10:46.760 --> 00:10:50.870
We do learn that Eugene Ottinger, the founding
member of the beekeeping club at Nevermore,

00:10:50.870 --> 00:10:51.870
has two mothers.

00:10:51.870 --> 00:10:55.700
Janet and Sue Ottinger visit Eugene when he
is injured in the hospital.

00:10:55.700 --> 00:11:01.115
This is the extent of the show's LGBTQ+ inclusion,
however, and it feels like it was barely thrown in.

00:11:01.115 --> 00:11:05.140
The minimum effort made is disappointing,
and we certainly hope that in Season 2, we'll

00:11:05.140 --> 00:11:06.450
see a big improvement.

